//RS /// Run a host transport with a hard stdout bound. The child is killed as soon
//RS /// as the bound is crossed, while stderr is drained on a helper thread so a
//RS /// noisy failed transport cannot deadlock the transfer. The caller receives
//RS /// only bounded bytes and a bounded diagnostic prefix.
